      "metadata": {
        "change_summary": "Replaced the kernel-vote field with an anisotropic nearest-distance (Voronoi) implicit field: f = min_neg - min_pos under metric (dx^2+dy^2)/A^2 + dz^2; horizontal stretch A chosen by leave-one-borehole-out IoU with compactness tie-break (default 2.5). Removes class-imbalance dilution; zero level set passes through contacts.",
        "harness_lineage": {
          "candidate_index": 0,
          "profile_id": "researcher_1",
          "session_id": "01a16cb3-f824-716f-b18b-1ef739692572",
          "submission_id": "researcher_1_round_1-submission-1",
          "turn_id": "researcher_1_round_1"
        },
        "parent_sha256": null,
        "rationale": "Diagnosed that Gaussian kernel-vote/ridge fields fail under the strong negative majority: CV selected lateral bandwidth ~0.4*domain and positive samples ended up with negative field values (empty masks, contact loss 4-5). A signed nearest-distance field is scale-free with respect to class prevalence, keeps the boundary on the pos/neg equidistant surface (hence near contacts), and adds a single interpretable anisotropy for layered geology. Public checks: legal, fast (<0.1 s), loss improves strongly on 1810d/e08d1/2999f/3d3d8/3a616 and matches baseline on 2fd5/b254d/eaf3c; per-case mean public loss 0.613 vs baseline 0.509, so lateral over-extension at large A is the known weakness to address next.",
        "research_fork": {
          "lineage_id": "explore_0001_researcher_1",
          "parent_id": "main_0001",
          "profile_id": "researcher_1",
          "purpose": "restart"
        }
      },
